    "content": "\"Cream Abdul-Jabbar\" is the popular nickname for Robbie Avila, a 6'10\" standout center for the Saint Louis University Billikens, known for his goggles, high-IQ play, and efficiency. After starring at Indiana State, he followed coach Josh Schertz to St. Louis, where he is a 2025-26 star in the NCAA Tournament. Key Details About \"Cream Abdul-Jabbar\" (Robbie Avila): The Nickname: Coined during his time at Indiana State, the nickname plays on his goggles and skilled, post-oriented game, often cited as a top nickname in college basketball. Other nicknames include \"Larry Nerd\" and \"College Jokic\". Move to St. Louis: Following a stellar sophomore season at Indiana State, Avila transferred to Saint Louis University (SLU) for the 2024-25 season to reunite with coach Josh Schertz. Playing Style: Known for being a highly skilled offensive center with excellent passing ability, shooting range, and post moves. Awards and Recognition: He was a finalist for the 2025 Kareem Abdul-Jabbar Center of the Year Award and earned All-MVC (2024) and All-Atlantic 10 (2025) honors. March Madness Impact: He led Saint Louis to the 2026 NCAA Tournament, bringing national attention to the team as a top scorer and playmaker.",
